 17592186045417] [17592186555673 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555673 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186555488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555673 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "45b92ccf-c96a-52fb-b618-ecc3a61419d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186555626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186555519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555731 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb51de07-a3ab-5b3e-aa1b-ded6bbcf5569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90603" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈3.314\\,81,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}(2x-5), & 3\\le x<5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15966dc5-b8d2-54f2-9092-584d157e0965" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555765 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{9}(2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{27}|}_{0}^{3}+{\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3})|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & ≈13.074\\,07\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈13.074\\,07-(3.314\\,81)^{2} \\\\  & ≈2.09\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.136\\,90,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0\\le x<1, \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{14}, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "42fc75dd-9bd8-5bf5-a346-8dddd7ab3b06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555796 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{14}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{14}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{70}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1.578\\,57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.578\\,57-(1.136\\,90)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{30(x-1)}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d36205bb-47f5-5c37-9085-d080474849b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555857 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{30(x-1)}{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{30x-30}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{30}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{30}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{30}{4{x}^{4}}+\\frac{30}{5{x}^{5}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2{x}^{4}}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{5}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{30(x-1)}{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{30x-30}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{30}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{30}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{30}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{30}{4{x}^{4}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{15}{2{x}^{4}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555877 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0d913b51-4d46-55e2-8d62-53eb1bef16a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555877 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186555857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555888 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "27cb2740-d0d9-5281-bada-08690bd45b88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555921 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555921 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89eecdb2-d635-5827-856f-b37cb0e945a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555921 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186555796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555932 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555932 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c4b6fd65-5ab7-5aa6-9e67-5234b1c48ef4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555932 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186555765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555947 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555947 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dfc975d2-2b17-5834-9ec2-f3d0328a5946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555947 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444792 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
